.TH MYSTRLEN 3
.SH NAME
mystrlen \- calculate the length of a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.br
.B int mystrlen(const char *s);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mystrlen
calculates the number of characters in the string pointed to by
.I s
before the terminating null character.
.PP
If
.I s
is NULL, the function returns -1.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the string length on success, or -1 when the input pointer is NULL.
.SH AUTHOR
Usman Hassan <usmaanhassan@outlook.com>
